    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296">

                <pb facs="0655" n="617" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv11/pg617"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Paris Peace Conf. 185.271/6: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Acting
                        Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-23T21:00:00+01:00">July 23, 1919—9
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>3278. [From White.] In order to ascertain whether Colonel House expected to
                    return to Paris to sign the Austrian Treaty, I telegraphed him on July
                        19,<anchor n="71" xml:id="d296-f1"/> at the instance of the Drafting
                    Committee who desired to know this definitely, in connection with the
                    preparation of the text. Colonel House has answered as follows: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“The Commission on Mandates will sit in London August 5, therefore I had
                            better not undertake returning to Paris to sign the Treaty with
                            Austria.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed>White</signed><lb/><hi rendition="#small-caps">Am</hi>[<hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">erican</hi>] <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
